{"additions":2960,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nA read-only **Procs** page (`5`) that answers \"what is running\" and \"who holds this port\" without leaving vig: a process tree with CPU / memory, the listening TCP / UDP ports with their owning process, and a per-process detail. Like every vig page it only inspects — no signals, no kill — and environment variables are never read or displayed.\n\n![procs demo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/td72/vig/feat/procs-view/assets/demo-procs.gif)\n\nCloses #93, closes #94, closes #95, closes #96, closes #97\n\n## Changes\n\n**Page (`src/procs/`, follows the Files / GitHub page blueprint)**\n- `state.rs` — `ProcsState: PageState` with `PaneShared` / `PaneSet` / `Tab`; pane ids, layout, tabs, bind and keys all come from the new `page \"procs\"` block in `assets/default.kdl`; `\"5\" \"page:procs\"` in `app { }`\n- `panes/processes.rs` — tree by `ppid` via `core::tree::nest_by`; columns PID / CPU% / MEM (RSS) / command; `s` cycles CPU → MEM → PID (shown in the pane title); `/` searches command lines; the selection follows the pid across refreshes and sort changes\n- `panes/ports.rs` — proto / address:port / PID / name; `Enter` jumps to the owning process (`PaneEvent::JumpToProcess`); rows the current user cannot see show `(no access)`; a missing tool or unsupported platform is a one-line notice in the pane\n- `panes/detail.rs` — PID, PPID (with parent name), user, state, uptime, CPU / MEM, wrapped command line, cwd, exe, children (pid + name), listening ports; privileged values render as `(no access)`; scroll survives refreshes of the same pid\n- `domain/snapshot.rs` — `sysinfo` (0.39, `system` + `user` features only; `environ` is never requested) on a persistent sampler thread so CPU% is a real delta; `domain/ports.rs` — `lsof -nP -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN -iUDP` (macOS) / `ss -tulnp` (Linux) parsed from text, `\\x20` unescaped, connected / unbound UDP sockets skipped\n\n**Refresh** — never blocks the UI: snapshot and ports are requested on `r` and every `procs-refresh-interval` (new top-level KDL node, default `\"2s\"`, `\"500ms\"` / `\"1.5s\"` accepted, at least 250 ms) while the page is active; results arrive over an mpsc channel drained in `drain_background()`; in-flight requests are not duplicated\n\n**Core touch points** — `PaneEvent::JumpToProcess(u32)`, `Config::procs_page()` / `procs_refresh_interval()` (+ validation in `with_user`), `procs-refresh-interval` accepted by the merger, `render_procs_header` / `render_procs_status_bar`, page registration in `main.rs`, `\"5\"` in the app-keymap regression test\n\n**Docs / demo** — README (en / ja) feature bullet, view-switch key and a Procs View section; `docs/config.md` schema, merge rules and pane / action tables; `tape/demo-procs.tape` + `assets/demo-procs.gif` (`mise run demo:procs`, part of `demo:all`)\n\n**Tests** — `lsof` / `ss` fixture parsing (hidden owners, spaces in names, connected / wildcard sockets), ppid tree ordering under each sort, sort cycling, selection-follows-pid, ports jump / no-access path, detail line rendering, interval parsing, KDL page ids / keys / bindings, and a live-snapshot smoke test that finds the test process itself\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Linux: only through the `ss -tulnp` fixture tests and `cfg!(target_os)` branching — not run on a Linux host\n- Behaviour with a very large process count (tree nesting is O(n²) per refresh; fine at ~900 processes here)\n- Windows: the ports pane shows the \"not supported on this platform\" notice; process listing is whatever `sysinfo` provides there\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":27,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-28T07:49:34Z","deletions":20,"headRefName":"feat/procs-view","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":109,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPIUxA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nIt introduces a large new cross-platform feature with background sampling and external command parsing, so it warrants careful human review despite the mostly solid structure.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds a new read-only **Procs** page (key `5`) to vig, providing an in-app process tree, listening ports ownership lookup, and per-process detail, integrated into the existing page/pane/keymap/config architecture.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces the `src/procs/` page (state + panes + domain samplers/parsers) and registers it in the app/UI.\n- Adds config support for `procs-refresh-interval` and merges it as a replaceable top-level KDL node.\n- Updates docs and demo assets/tapes to document and showcase the new Procs view.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `tape/demo-procs.tape` | New VHS tape to record the Procs view demo GIF. |\r\n| `src/procs/state.rs` | Procs page state, background refresh wiring, pane set wiring, and page-level tests. |\r\n| `src/procs/panes/processes.rs` | Processes pane: tree, sorting, selection-following, and search. |\r\n| `src/procs/panes/ports.rs` | Ports pane: listing, search, and jump-to-process behavior. |\r\n| `src/procs/panes/detail.rs` | Detail pane: field rendering, wrapping, and scroll behavior. |\r\n| `src/procs/panes/mod.rs` | Shared Procs pane utilities (table pane renderer, truncation helpers). |\r\n| `src/procs/page.rs` | Page constructor for Procs. |\r\n| `src/procs/mod.rs` | Module wiring for the new Procs feature. |\r\n| `src/procs/domain/types.rs` | Snapshot data types and sort helpers for processes/ports. |\r\n| `src/procs/domain/snapshot.rs` | `sysinfo`-based background sampler for process snapshots (CPU delta-aware). |\r\n| `src/procs/domain/ports.rs` | `lsof`/`ss` execution and fixture-testable parsing for listening ports. |\r\n| `src/procs/domain/mod.rs` | Domain module exports for Procs. |\r\n| `src/main.rs` | Registers the Procs page in the main page list. |\r\n| `src/core/ui/status_bar.rs` | Adds Procs header/status bar renderers (counts + refresh indicator). |\r\n| `src/core/pane.rs` | Adds `PaneEvent::JumpToProcess(u32)` for ports → processes navigation. |\r\n| `src/core/config/merge.rs` | Allows `procs-refresh-interval` as a replaceable top-level config node. |\r\n| `src/core/config/loader.rs` | Adds interval parsing + `Config::procs_page()` and `Config::procs_refresh_interval()` validation/tests. |\r\n| `src/core/app.rs` | App keymap regression test updated to include Procs page switching. |\r\n| `README.md` | Documents the new Procs View and its keybindings. |\r\n| `docs/README.ja.md` | Japanese docs update for Procs View and keybindings. |\r\n| `docs/config.md` | Documents `procs-refresh-interval` and adds `procs` to page/key tables. |\r\n| `mise.toml` | Adds `demo:procs` and includes it in `demo:all`. |\r\n| `Cargo.toml` | Adds `sysinfo` dependency (limited features). |\r\n| `Cargo.lock` | Locks dependency additions for `sysinfo` and transitive crates. |\r\n| `assets/demo-procs.gif` | New Git LFS-tracked Procs demo GIF. |\r\n| `assets/default.kdl` | Adds `procs-refresh-interval`, Procs page block, and binds key `5` to `page:procs`. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 25/26 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T07:52:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"36cc2c9260ed6c01b95160f621b323106e5ff7ce"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPKBGg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nIt introduces a few concrete correctness/usability issues (in-app help lists an unbound key, and the demo tape teardown relies on job control) plus a resource-usage concern (spawning a new thread per ports refresh).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (5)\n\n**Previously missed (1)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**tape/demo-procs.tape:30**\n* The demo tape starts the HTTP server in the background but doesn't capture its PID, and the teardown uses `kill %1` (job control), which can fail in non-interactive shells. Capture `$!` when starting the server so teardown can reliably `kill` the right process.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 98 of the same file.\n```\n# Something for the Ports pane to find: an HTTP server owned by this shell.\nType@1ms \"python3 -m http.server 8765 >/dev/null 2>&1 &\"\nEnter\nSleep 1s\n```\n\n**src/procs/state.rs:291**\n* The help overlay lists `4` as a view-switch key, but the default config binds only `1`, `2`, `3`, and `5` (no `4`). This makes the in-app help inaccurate.\n```\n        let s = |k: &str, v: &str| (k.to_string(), v.to_string());\n        let mut entries = vec![s(\"1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5\", \"Switch view\")];\n        entries.extend(self.view_keymap.help_entries());\n```\n**src/procs/state.rs:506**\n* This test asserts the same incorrect view-switch key list (includes `4` even though it isn't bound by default), so it will lock in the inaccurate help text.\n```\n        let s = state();\n        let help = s.help_bindings();\n        assert_eq!(help[0].0, \"1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5\");\n        let text: Vec<String> = help.iter().map(|(k, v)| format!(\"{k} {v}\")).collect();\n```\n**src/procs/state.rs:197**\n* `request_refresh()` spawns a new OS thread for every ports refresh. With a minimum refresh interval of 250ms, this can create a steady stream of short-lived threads and add overhead over long sessions. Consider reusing a single long-lived worker (similar to `snapshot::spawn_worker`) driven by a request channel.\n```\n        if !self.ports_pending {\n            if let Some(tx) = &self.bg_tx {\n                self.ports_pending = true;\n                let tx = tx.clone();\n                std::thread::spawn(move || {\n                    let _ = tx.send(ProcsBgMessage::Ports(ports::fetch_ports()));\n                });\n            }\n```\n**tape/demo-procs.tape:101**\n* Teardown uses `kill %1`, which depends on job control and may not work in this recording environment. Prefer killing the captured PID from the setup step.\n```\n# --- Hidden teardown: stop the server ---\nHide\nType@1ms \"kill %1\"\nEnter\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 25/26 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T07:56:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"cbad8e19ea689b9a54f9cf9588e3b435d8c0078f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPVOTw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:19:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"cbad8e19ea689b9a54f9cf9588e3b435d8c0078f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPVPJg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:19:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"cbad8e19ea689b9a54f9cf9588e3b435d8c0078f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPVQQw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:19:06Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"cbad8e19ea689b9a54f9cf9588e3b435d8c0078f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPa4rA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\n`parse_interval` can accept below-minimum values due to rounding behavior, and the Procs state module docs currently contradict the intended env-var usage.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 26/27 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:31:11Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"fcd2ec2a19c23ccd99ec2aed9c9be267f92d7626"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:30:09Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155591052/job/98797474886","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:30:10Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:29:33Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155465569/job/98797076096","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:28:21Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:28:46Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155465513/job/98797075956","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:28:21Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:29:21Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155465569/job/98797076132","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:28:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:29:57Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155465569/job/98797075943","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:28:21Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:29:57Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155465569/job/98797427032","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:29:57Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:30:09Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155591052/job/98797474676","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:30:10Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:29:07Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155465513/job/98797076052","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:28:22Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:29:35Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155465513/job/98797075718","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:28:21Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:30:09Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33155591052/job/98797475040","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:30:10Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Procs view: process tree, listening ports and process detail"}
